module

public import ConicalKahler.Cone.Standard
public import Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.ExpDeriv
public import Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Deriv
public import Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals.Basic
public import Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Log

/-!
# The standard cone metric is the flat cone of angle `2πβ`

This file proves the metric-geometric meaning of the model. The standard cone metric
`ω_β = i β² |z_0|^(2β-2) dz_0 ∧ dz̄_0 + i ∑_{j ≥ 1} dz_j ∧ dz̄_j` is the Riemannian product of a
**transverse** metric in the `z_0`-direction and the flat metric of `ℂⁿ⁻¹`
(`modelConeQuadratic_single_eq_transverse`). The transverse metric is *exactly* (isometrically,
not merely up to a constant) the flat cone of angle `2πβ`.

## The flat cone of angle `2πβ`

On `(0, ∞) × ℝ` with coordinates `(ρ, φ)` consider the metric `dρ² + ρ² dφ²` (`flatConeMetric`).

* It is flat: it is the pullback of the Euclidean metric `|dw|²` by the local diffeomorphism
  `(ρ, φ) ↦ ρ e^{iφ}` (`flatConeMetric_eq_normSq_fderiv_polarMap`).
* The translation `φ ↦ φ + 2πβ` is an isometry of it, and develops to the rotation
  `w ↦ e^{2πiβ} w` of the plane (`polarMap_add_snd`).

The **flat cone of angle `2πβ`** is the quotient of `(0, ∞) × ℝ` by `φ ~ φ + 2πβ`. Equivalently it
is the quotient of the universal cover of `ℂ \ {0}` with its flat metric by the rotation through
`2πβ`. For `β ∉ ℤ` this rotation is nontrivial (`exp_two_pi_mul_I_eq_one_iff`).

## The isometry

Write a point of `ℂ \ {0}` in polar coordinates `z_0 = r e^{iθ}` (`polarMap`). The universal
cover is `(r, θ) ∈ (0, ∞) × ℝ` and the deck group is generated by `θ ↦ θ + 2π`. The **radial change
of variables**

  `ρ = c r^β`, `φ = β θ`  (`coneRadialChange c β`)

is a diffeomorphism of `(0, ∞) × ℝ` (`coneRadialChangeHomeomorph`,
`contDiffOn_coneRadialChange`, `contDiffOn_coneRadialChangeInv`). It conjugates `θ ↦ θ + 2π` to
`φ ↦ φ + 2πβ` (`coneRadialChange_add_two_pi`), so it descends to a diffeomorphism from `ℂ \ {0}`
onto the flat cone of angle `2πβ`. The main theorems say that it is an **isometry**:

* `transverseConeMetric_polar` (Hermitian normalisation, `c = 1`): in polar coordinates the
  transverse Hermitian form `β² |z_0|^(2β-2) |dz_0|²` is exactly `dρ² + ρ² dφ²` with `ρ = r^β`.
* `standardConeForm_polar_riemannian` (Riemannian normalisation, `c = √2`): on every transverse
  slice `{z' = const}` the Riemannian metric `g(v, v) = ω_β(v, Jv)` of the *actual* Kähler form
  `standardConeForm β` is exactly `dρ² + ρ² dφ²` with `ρ = √2 r^β`, `φ = βθ`. The factor `√2` is
  the upstream normalisation `g = 2 × (Hermitian form)` (see the README). It is a dilation, which
  is an isometry between cones of the same angle.

`transverseConeMetric_exp` gives the same fact in complex-analytic form: on the universal cover
`exp : ℂ → ℂ \ {0}`, the transverse metric is the pullback of the Euclidean metric by the
developing map `ζ ↦ e^{βζ}` (locally `w = z_0^β`), whose holonomy is the rotation by `2πβ`
(`exp_mul_add_two_pi_I`).

## Metric invariants

`radialLength_eq` and `circleLength_eq`: the segment from the vertex to `|z_0| = r` has length
`r^β`, and the circle `|z_0| = r` has length `2πβ r^β` (`circleLength_eq_two_pi_mul_radialLength`).
The ratio is the cone angle `2πβ`. Lengths are those of the Hermitian form. With the Riemannian
normalisation both lengths get the same factor `√2`.

## Relation to the quasi-isometric cone condition

All statements here are **equalities** of metric tensors. They are properties of the model alone.
The quasi-isometric cone condition `IsConeAlong` only bounds a metric between `C⁻¹` and `C` times
the model in some adapted chart. It does not imply that the metric is a flat cone, even
asymptotically or transversally. `ConicalKahler.Cone.QuasiIsometricExample` gives a Kähler metric
that satisfies `IsConeAlong` but is not Ricci-flat, so it is not locally isometric to the model.
-/

@[expose] public section

open scoped Manifold ContDiff Topology Real
open Set Filter

namespace ConicalKahler

/-! ### Polar coordinates -/

/-- Polar coordinates `(r, θ) ↦ r e^{iθ}` on `ℂ`. On `(0, ∞) × ℝ` this is the universal covering of
`ℂ \ {0}`, and its deck group is generated by `θ ↦ θ + 2π`. In the coordinates `(ρ, φ)` of the
flat cone it is the developing map `(ρ, φ) ↦ ρ e^{iφ}`. -/
noncomputable def polarMap (x : ℝ × ℝ) : ℂ :=
  (x.1 : ℂ) * Complex.exp (x.2 * Complex.I)

theorem hasFDerivAt_polarMap (x : ℝ × ℝ) :
    HasFDerivAt polarMap
      ((x.1 : ℂ) • (Complex.exp (x.2 * Complex.I) •
          (Complex.I • (Complex.ofRealCLM.comp (ContinuousLinearMap.snd ℝ ℝ ℝ)))) +
        Complex.exp (x.2 * Complex.I) • (Complex.ofRealCLM.comp (ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ)))
      x := by
  have h1 : HasFDerivAt (fun x : ℝ × ℝ => (x.1 : ℂ))
      (Complex.ofRealCLM.comp (ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ)) x :=
    Complex.ofRealCLM.hasFDerivAt.comp x hasFDerivAt_fst
  have h2 : HasFDerivAt (fun x : ℝ × ℝ => (x.2 : ℂ) * Complex.I)
      (Complex.I • (Complex.ofRealCLM.comp (ContinuousLinearMap.snd ℝ ℝ ℝ))) x := by
    have := (Complex.ofRealCLM.hasFDerivAt.comp x hasFDerivAt_snd).mul_const Complex.I
    convert this using 1
    ext u
    simp [mul_comm]
  exact h1.mul h2.cexp

/-- `D(r e^{iθ})(dr, dθ) = (dr + i r dθ) e^{iθ}`. -/
theorem fderiv_polarMap (x u : ℝ × ℝ) :
    fderiv ℝ polarMap x u = (u.1 + x.1 * u.2 * Complex.I) * Complex.exp (x.2 * Complex.I) := by
  rw [(hasFDerivAt_polarMap x).fderiv]
  simp
  ring

/-- `|D(r e^{iθ})(dr, dθ)|² = dr² + r² dθ²`: the Euclidean metric in polar coordinates. -/
theorem normSq_fderiv_polarMap (x u : ℝ × ℝ) :
    Complex.normSq (fderiv ℝ polarMap x u) = u.1 ^ 2 + x.1 ^ 2 * u.2 ^ 2 := by
  rw [fderiv_polarMap, Complex.normSq_mul, Complex.normSq_eq_norm_sq (Complex.exp _),
    Complex.norm_exp_ofReal_mul_I]
  simp [Complex.normSq_apply]
  ring

theorem norm_polarMap (x : ℝ × ℝ) : ‖polarMap x‖ = |x.1| := by
  simp [polarMap, Complex.norm_exp_ofReal_mul_I]

theorem norm_polarMap_of_nonneg {x : ℝ × ℝ} (hr : 0 ≤ x.1) : ‖polarMap x‖ = x.1 := by
  rw [norm_polarMap, abs_of_nonneg hr]

theorem polarMap_ne_zero {x : ℝ × ℝ} (hr : 0 < x.1) : polarMap x ≠ 0 := by
  rw [← norm_ne_zero_iff, norm_polarMap_of_nonneg hr.le]
  exact hr.ne'

/-- Rotating the angle by `α` rotates the point by `e^{iα}`. -/
theorem polarMap_add_snd (ρ φ α : ℝ) :
    polarMap (ρ, φ + α) = Complex.exp (α * Complex.I) * polarMap (ρ, φ) := by
  simp only [polarMap, Complex.ofReal_add, add_mul, Complex.exp_add]
  ring

/-- The deck transformation `θ ↦ θ + 2π` of the universal covering of `ℂ \ {0}`. -/
theorem polarMap_add_two_pi (r θ : ℝ) : polarMap (r, θ + 2 * π) = polarMap (r, θ) := by
  rw [polarMap_add_snd]
  have : Complex.exp ((2 * π : ℝ) * Complex.I) = 1 := by
    rw [Complex.exp_eq_one_iff]
    exact ⟨1, by push_cast; ring⟩
  rw [this, one_mul]

/-- Every nonzero complex number has polar coordinates with `r > 0`. -/
theorem exists_polarMap_eq {z : ℂ} (hz : z ≠ 0) : ∃ x : ℝ × ℝ, 0 < x.1 ∧ polarMap x = z :=
  ⟨(‖z‖, Complex.arg z), norm_pos_iff.mpr hz, by
    simp only [polarMap]
    exact Complex.norm_mul_exp_arg_mul_I z⟩

/-! ### The flat cone -/

/-- The flat cone metric `dρ² + ρ² dφ²` at the point `y = (ρ, φ)` on the tangent vector
`u = (dρ, dφ)`. On `(0, ∞) × ℝ` modulo `φ ~ φ + 2πβ` it is the **flat cone of angle `2πβ`**. -/
def flatConeMetric (y u : ℝ × ℝ) : ℝ :=
  u.1 ^ 2 + y.1 ^ 2 * u.2 ^ 2

/-- **The cone is flat.** The cone metric is the pullback of the Euclidean metric `|dw|²` of `ℂ`
by the developing map `(ρ, φ) ↦ ρ e^{iφ}`. -/
theorem flatConeMetric_eq_normSq_fderiv_polarMap (y u : ℝ × ℝ) :
    flatConeMetric y u = Complex.normSq (fderiv ℝ polarMap y u) := by
  rw [normSq_fderiv_polarMap, flatConeMetric]

/-- The identification `φ ~ φ + α` is an isometry of the cone metric. -/
theorem flatConeMetric_add_snd (ρ φ α : ℝ) (u : ℝ × ℝ) :
    flatConeMetric (ρ, φ + α) u = flatConeMetric (ρ, φ) u :=
  rfl

theorem flatConeMetric_nonneg (y u : ℝ × ℝ) : 0 ≤ flatConeMetric y u := by
  unfold flatConeMetric
  positivity

/-- The flat cone metric is positive definite away from the vertex. -/
theorem flatConeMetric_pos {y u : ℝ × ℝ} (hy : y.1 ≠ 0) (hu : u ≠ 0) : 0 < flatConeMetric y u := by
  unfold flatConeMetric
  rcases eq_or_ne u.1 0 with h1 | h1
  · have h2 : u.2 ≠ 0 := fun h2 => hu (Prod.ext h1 h2)
    have : 0 < y.1 ^ 2 * u.2 ^ 2 := by positivity
    nlinarith [sq_nonneg u.1]
  · have : 0 < u.1 ^ 2 := by positivity
    nlinarith [sq_nonneg y.1, sq_nonneg u.2, mul_nonneg (sq_nonneg y.1) (sq_nonneg u.2)]

/-- A dilation `ρ ↦ cρ` multiplies the cone metric by `c²`. In particular `c² (dρ² + ρ² dφ²)` is
again a flat cone of the same angle. -/
theorem flatConeMetric_dilate (c : ℝ) (y u : ℝ × ℝ) :
    flatConeMetric (c * y.1, y.2) (c * u.1, u.2) = c ^ 2 * flatConeMetric y u := by
  unfold flatConeMetric
  ring

/-! ### The radial change of variables -/

/-- The radial change of variables `(r, θ) ↦ (c r^β, β θ)` from polar coordinates on `ℂ \ {0}` to
polar coordinates `(ρ, φ)` on the cone. -/
noncomputable def coneRadialChange (c β : ℝ) (x : ℝ × ℝ) : ℝ × ℝ :=
  (c * x.1 ^ β, β * x.2)

/-- Its inverse `(ρ, φ) ↦ ((ρ / c)^(1/β), φ / β)`. -/
noncomputable def coneRadialChangeInv (c β : ℝ) (y : ℝ × ℝ) : ℝ × ℝ :=
  ((y.1 / c) ^ β⁻¹, y.2 / β)

/-- The open half-plane `(0, ∞) × ℝ` of polar coordinates away from the vertex. -/
def polarDomain : Set (ℝ × ℝ) :=
  Ioi 0 ×ˢ univ

theorem isOpen_polarDomain : IsOpen polarDomain :=
  isOpen_Ioi.prod isOpen_univ

@[simp]
theorem mem_polarDomain {x : ℝ × ℝ} : x ∈ polarDomain ↔ 0 < x.1 := by
  simp [polarDomain]

section RadialChange

variable {c β : ℝ}

/-- **Equivariance.** The deck transformation `θ ↦ θ + 2π` of `ℂ \ {0}` becomes `φ ↦ φ + 2πβ`.
So the radial change descends to a map from `ℂ \ {0}` onto the flat cone of angle `2πβ`. -/
theorem coneRadialChange_add_two_pi (r θ : ℝ) :
    coneRadialChange c β (r, θ + 2 * π) = coneRadialChange c β (r, θ) + (0, 2 * π * β) := by
  simp only [coneRadialChange, Prod.mk_add_mk, add_zero, Prod.mk.injEq, true_and]
  ring

theorem coneRadialChange_mapsTo (hc : 0 < c) :
    MapsTo (coneRadialChange c β) polarDomain polarDomain := fun x hx => by
  rw [mem_polarDomain] at hx ⊢
  exact mul_pos hc (Real.rpow_pos_of_pos hx _)

theorem coneRadialChangeInv_mapsTo (hc : 0 < c) :
    MapsTo (coneRadialChangeInv c β) polarDomain polarDomain := fun y hy => by
  rw [mem_polarDomain] at hy ⊢
  exact Real.rpow_pos_of_pos (div_pos hy hc) _

theorem coneRadialChangeInv_coneRadialChange (hc : 0 < c) (hβ : β ≠ 0) {x : ℝ × ℝ}
    (hx : x ∈ polarDomain) : coneRadialChangeInv c β (coneRadialChange c β x) = x := by
  rw [mem_polarDomain] at hx
  simp only [coneRadialChange, coneRadialChangeInv]
  ext
  · simp only
    rw [mul_div_cancel_left₀ _ hc.ne', ← Real.rpow_mul hx.le, mul_inv_cancel₀ hβ, Real.rpow_one]
  · simp only
    field_simp

theorem coneRadialChange_coneRadialChangeInv (hc : 0 < c) (hβ : β ≠ 0) {y : ℝ × ℝ}
    (hy : y ∈ polarDomain) : coneRadialChange c β (coneRadialChangeInv c β y) = y := by
  rw [mem_polarDomain] at hy
  simp only [coneRadialChange, coneRadialChangeInv]
  ext
  · simp only
    rw [← Real.rpow_mul (div_pos hy hc).le, inv_mul_cancel₀ hβ, Real.rpow_one,
      mul_div_cancel₀ _ hc.ne']
  · simp only
    field_simp

theorem contDiffOn_coneRadialChange {m : WithTop ℕ∞} :
    ContDiffOn ℝ m (coneRadialChange c β) polarDomain := by
  intro x hx
  rw [mem_polarDomain] at hx
  refine ContDiffAt.contDiffWithinAt ?_
  exact (contDiffAt_const.mul ((Real.contDiffAt_rpow_const_of_ne hx.ne').comp x
    contDiffAt_fst)).prodMk (contDiffAt_const.mul contDiffAt_snd)

theorem contDiffOn_coneRadialChangeInv (hc : 0 < c) {m : WithTop ℕ∞} :
    ContDiffOn ℝ m (coneRadialChangeInv c β) polarDomain := by
  intro y hy
  rw [mem_polarDomain] at hy
  refine ContDiffAt.contDiffWithinAt ?_
  exact ((Real.contDiffAt_rpow_const_of_ne (div_pos hy hc).ne').comp y
    (contDiffAt_fst.div_const c)).prodMk (contDiffAt_snd.div_const β)

/-- **The radial change of variables is a diffeomorphism of `(0, ∞) × ℝ`** (for `c, β > 0`),
bundled as a homeomorphism between open subsets. Smoothness of it and its inverse is
`contDiffOn_coneRadialChange` and `contDiffOn_coneRadialChangeInv`. -/
noncomputable def coneRadialChangeHomeomorph (hc : 0 < c) (hβ : 0 < β) :
    OpenPartialHomeomorph (ℝ × ℝ) (ℝ × ℝ) where
  toFun := coneRadialChange c β
  invFun := coneRadialChangeInv c β
  source := polarDomain
  target := polarDomain
  map_source' := coneRadialChange_mapsTo hc
  map_target' := coneRadialChangeInv_mapsTo hc
  left_inv' _ hx := coneRadialChangeInv_coneRadialChange hc hβ.ne' hx
  right_inv' _ hy := coneRadialChange_coneRadialChangeInv hc hβ.ne' hy
  open_source := isOpen_polarDomain
  open_target := isOpen_polarDomain
  continuousOn_toFun := (contDiffOn_coneRadialChange (m := 0)).continuousOn
  continuousOn_invFun := (contDiffOn_coneRadialChangeInv hc (m := 0)).continuousOn

theorem hasFDerivAt_coneRadialChange {x : ℝ × ℝ} (hx : 0 < x.1) :
    HasFDerivAt (coneRadialChange c β)
      (((c * (β * x.1 ^ (β - 1))) • ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ).prod
        (β • ContinuousLinearMap.snd ℝ ℝ ℝ)) x := by
  have h1 : HasFDerivAt (fun x : ℝ × ℝ => x.1 ^ β)
      ((β * x.1 ^ (β - 1)) • ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ) x :=
    (Real.hasDerivAt_rpow_const (Or.inl hx.ne')).comp_hasFDerivAt x hasFDerivAt_fst
  have h2 : HasFDerivAt (fun x : ℝ × ℝ => β * x.2) (β • ContinuousLinearMap.snd ℝ ℝ ℝ) x := by
    simpa using (hasFDerivAt_snd (p := x)).const_mul β
  have h1' : HasFDerivAt (fun x : ℝ × ℝ => c * x.1 ^ β)
      ((c * (β * x.1 ^ (β - 1))) • ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ) x := by
    simpa [smul_smul] using h1.const_mul c
  exact h1'.prodMk h2

/-- `D(c r^β, βθ)(dr, dθ) = (c β r^(β-1) dr, β dθ)`. -/
theorem fderiv_coneRadialChange {x : ℝ × ℝ} (hx : 0 < x.1) (u : ℝ × ℝ) :
    fderiv ℝ (coneRadialChange c β) x u = (c * (β * x.1 ^ (β - 1)) * u.1, β * u.2) := by
  rw [(hasFDerivAt_coneRadialChange hx).fderiv]
  simp

/-- The pullback of the flat cone metric by the radial change:
`d(c r^β)² + (c r^β)² d(βθ)² = c² β² r^(2β-2) (dr² + r² dθ²)`. -/
theorem flatConeMetric_coneRadialChange {x : ℝ × ℝ} (hx : 0 < x.1) (u : ℝ × ℝ) :
    flatConeMetric (coneRadialChange c β x) (fderiv ℝ (coneRadialChange c β) x u) =
      c ^ 2 * β ^ 2 * x.1 ^ (2 * β - 2) * (u.1 ^ 2 + x.1 ^ 2 * u.2 ^ 2) := by
  rw [fderiv_coneRadialChange hx, flatConeMetric, coneRadialChange]
  simp only
  have h1 : (x.1 ^ (β - 1)) ^ 2 = x.1 ^ (2 * β - 2) := by
    rw [← Real.rpow_natCast, ← Real.rpow_mul hx.le]
    norm_num
    ring_nf
  have h2 : (x.1 ^ β) ^ 2 = x.1 ^ (2 * β - 2) * x.1 ^ 2 := by
    rw [← Real.rpow_natCast, ← Real.rpow_mul hx.le, ← Real.rpow_natCast x.1 2,
      ← Real.rpow_add hx]
    norm_num
    ring_nf
  calc (c * (β * x.1 ^ (β - 1)) * u.1) ^ 2 + (c * x.1 ^ β) ^ 2 * (β * u.2) ^ 2
      = c ^ 2 * β ^ 2 * (x.1 ^ (β - 1)) ^ 2 * u.1 ^ 2 + c ^ 2 * β ^ 2 * (x.1 ^ β) ^ 2 * u.2 ^ 2 := by
        ring
    _ = _ := by rw [h1, h2]; ring

end RadialChange

/-! ### The transverse cone metric -/

/-- The Hermitian quadratic form `β² |ζ|^(2β-2) |w|²` of the transverse factor
`i β² |ζ|^(2β-2) dζ ∧ dζ̄` of `ω_β`, at the point `ζ ∈ ℂ` on the tangent vector `w`. -/
noncomputable def transverseConeMetric (β : ConeAngle) (ζ w : ℂ) : ℝ :=
  β.beta ^ 2 * ‖ζ‖ ^ (2 * β.beta - 2) * Complex.normSq w

/-- **Product structure.** The model quadratic form of `ω_β` is the transverse cone metric in
`z_0` plus the flat metric in `z' = (z_1, …, z_{n-1})`. -/
theorem modelConeQuadratic_single_eq_transverse {n : ℕ} [NeZero n] (β : ConeAngle) (z v : E n) :
    modelConeQuadratic (singleConeWeights β) z v =
      transverseConeMetric β (z 0) (v 0) + ∑ j ∈ Finset.univ.erase 0, Complex.normSq (v j) := by
  rw [modelConeQuadratic, ← Finset.add_sum_erase _ _ (Finset.mem_univ 0), modelWeight_single_zero]
  congr 1
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j hj => by
    rw [modelWeight_single_of_ne β z (Finset.ne_of_mem_erase hj), one_mul]

/-- **The transverse metric is the flat cone of angle `2πβ`** (Hermitian normalisation). In polar
coordinates `ζ = r e^{iθ}`, `r > 0`, the transverse cone metric is the pullback of
`dρ² + ρ² dφ²` by the radial change of variables `ρ = r^β`, `φ = βθ`:

  `β² |ζ|^(2β-2) |dζ|² = d(r^β)² + r^(2β) d(βθ)²`. -/
theorem transverseConeMetric_polar (β : ConeAngle) {x : ℝ × ℝ} (hx : 0 < x.1) (u : ℝ × ℝ) :
    transverseConeMetric β (polarMap x) (fderiv ℝ polarMap x u) =
      flatConeMetric (coneRadialChange 1 β.beta x) (fderiv ℝ (coneRadialChange 1 β.beta) x u) := by
  rw [flatConeMetric_coneRadialChange hx, transverseConeMetric, norm_polarMap_of_nonneg hx.le,
    normSq_fderiv_polarMap]
  ring

/-! ### The actual Kähler form on a transverse slice -/

section Slice

variable {n : ℕ} [NeZero n]

/-- The transverse slice through `w`: `ζ ↦ (ζ, w_1, …, w_{n-1})`. -/
noncomputable def transverseSlice (w : E n) (ζ : ℂ) : E n :=
  w + (ζ - w 0) • EuclideanSpace.single 0 1

@[simp]
theorem transverseSlice_apply_zero (w : E n) (ζ : ℂ) : transverseSlice w ζ 0 = ζ := by
  simp [transverseSlice]

theorem transverseSlice_apply_of_ne (w : E n) (ζ : ℂ) {j : Fin n} (hj : j ≠ 0) :
    transverseSlice w ζ j = w j := by
  simp [transverseSlice, hj]

theorem transverseSlice_mem_modelDomain (β : ConeAngle) (w : E n) {x : ℝ × ℝ} (hx : 0 < x.1) :
    transverseSlice w (polarMap x) ∈ modelDomain (singleConeWeights β) := by
  rw [mem_modelDomain_single, transverseSlice_apply_zero]
  exact polarMap_ne_zero hx

theorem hasFDerivAt_transverseSlice (w : E n) (ζ : ℂ) :
    HasFDerivAt (transverseSlice w)
      ((ContinuousLinearMap.id ℝ ℂ).smulRight (EuclideanSpace.single (0 : Fin n) (1 : ℂ))) ζ := by
  have h := ((hasFDerivAt_id (𝕜 := ℝ) ζ).sub_const (w 0)).smul_const
    (EuclideanSpace.single (0 : Fin n) (1 : ℂ))
  exact h.const_add w

/-- The velocity of the polar-coordinate curve in a transverse slice: only the `z_0`-component
moves. -/
theorem fderiv_transverseSlice_polarMap (w : E n) (x u : ℝ × ℝ) :
    fderiv ℝ (transverseSlice w ∘ polarMap) x u =
      fderiv ℝ polarMap x u • EuclideanSpace.single (0 : Fin n) (1 : ℂ) := by
  rw [((hasFDerivAt_transverseSlice w (polarMap x)).comp x (hasFDerivAt_polarMap x)).fderiv,
    ← (hasFDerivAt_polarMap x).fderiv]
  simp

/-- The Hermitian quadratic form of `ω_β` on a transverse slice, in polar coordinates, is exactly
the flat cone metric under `ρ = r^β`, `φ = βθ`. -/
theorem modelConeQuadratic_polar_slice (β : ConeAngle) (w : E n) {x : ℝ × ℝ} (hx : 0 < x.1)
    (u : ℝ × ℝ) :
    modelConeQuadratic (singleConeWeights β) (transverseSlice w (polarMap x))
        (fderiv ℝ (transverseSlice w ∘ polarMap) x u) =
      flatConeMetric (coneRadialChange 1 β.beta x) (fderiv ℝ (coneRadialChange 1 β.beta) x u) := by
  rw [modelConeQuadratic_single_eq_transverse, fderiv_transverseSlice_polarMap,
    transverseSlice_apply_zero, ← transverseConeMetric_polar β hx]
  have hrest : ∑ j ∈ Finset.univ.erase (0 : Fin n),
      Complex.normSq ((fderiv ℝ polarMap x u • EuclideanSpace.single (0 : Fin n) (1 : ℂ)) j) =
        0 :=
    Finset.sum_eq_zero fun j hj => by
      simp [Finset.ne_of_mem_erase hj]
  rw [hrest, add_zero]
  simp

/-- **The transverse Riemannian metric of `ω_β` is the flat cone of angle `2πβ`.** Fix the
tangential coordinates `z' = (w_1, …, w_{n-1})` and write `z_0 = r e^{iθ}`, `r > 0`. Let `Γ` be
the resulting map `(r, θ) ↦ (r e^{iθ}, w_1, …, w_{n-1})`. The Riemannian metric
`g(v, v) = ω_β(v, Jv)` of the upstream Kähler form `standardConeForm β`, pulled back by `Γ`, is
exactly the flat cone metric `dρ² + ρ² dφ²` pulled back by the radial change of variables
`ρ = √2 r^β`, `φ = βθ`. The factor `√2` comes from the upstream convention `g = 2 Re h` (see the
README). -/
theorem standardConeForm_polar_riemannian (β : ConeAngle) (w : E n) {x : ℝ × ℝ} (hx : 0 < x.1)
    (u : ℝ × ℝ) :
    standardConeForm β ⟨transverseSlice w (polarMap x), transverseSlice_mem_modelDomain β w hx⟩
        ![fderiv ℝ (transverseSlice w ∘ polarMap) x u,
          Complex.I • fderiv ℝ (transverseSlice w ∘ polarMap) x u] =
      flatConeMetric (coneRadialChange (√2) β.beta x)
        (fderiv ℝ (coneRadialChange (√2) β.beta) x u) := by
  rw [modelConeForm_apply_I_smul]
  change 2 * modelConeQuadratic (singleConeWeights β) (transverseSlice w (polarMap x))
      (fderiv ℝ (transverseSlice w ∘ polarMap) x u) = _
  rw [modelConeQuadratic_polar_slice β w hx, flatConeMetric_coneRadialChange hx,
    flatConeMetric_coneRadialChange hx, Real.sq_sqrt (by norm_num : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 2)]
  ring

end Slice

/-! ### Developing map and holonomy -/

/-- **Developing map.** On the universal cover `exp : ℂ → ℂ \ {0}`, the transverse cone metric is
the pullback of the Euclidean metric `|dw|²` by the developing map `ζ ↦ e^{βζ}` (locally
`w = z_0^β`). In Kähler terms, `exp^* ω_β = (e^{β·})^* (i dw ∧ dw̄)` in the `z_0`-direction. -/
theorem transverseConeMetric_exp (β : ConeAngle) (ζ v : ℂ) :
    transverseConeMetric β (Complex.exp ζ) (deriv Complex.exp ζ * v) =
      Complex.normSq (deriv (fun ζ => Complex.exp (β.beta * ζ)) ζ * v) := by
  have hdev : deriv (fun ζ => Complex.exp (β.beta * ζ)) ζ = β.beta * Complex.exp (β.beta * ζ) := by
    have h := ((hasDerivAt_id' ζ).const_mul (β.beta : ℂ)).cexp
    rw [h.deriv]
    ring
  rw [hdev, Complex.deriv_exp, transverseConeMetric, Complex.norm_exp, Complex.normSq_mul,
    Complex.normSq_mul, Complex.normSq_mul, Complex.normSq_ofReal,
    Complex.normSq_eq_norm_sq (Complex.exp _), Complex.normSq_eq_norm_sq (Complex.exp _),
    Complex.norm_exp, Complex.norm_exp, ← Real.exp_mul, ← Real.exp_nat_mul, ← Real.exp_nat_mul]
  have hre : (β.beta * ζ : ℂ).re = β.beta * ζ.re := by simp
  rw [hre]
  have : Real.exp (ζ.re * (2 * β.beta - 2)) * Real.exp ((2 : ℕ) * ζ.re) =
      Real.exp ((2 : ℕ) * (β.beta * ζ.re)) := by
    rw [← Real.exp_add]
    congr 1
    push_cast
    ring
  calc β.beta ^ 2 * Real.exp (ζ.re * (2 * β.beta - 2)) *
        (Real.exp ((2 : ℕ) * ζ.re) * Complex.normSq v)
      = β.beta ^ 2 * (Real.exp (ζ.re * (2 * β.beta - 2)) * Real.exp ((2 : ℕ) * ζ.re)) *
          Complex.normSq v := by ring
    _ = _ := by rw [this]; ring

/-- The deck transformation `ζ ↦ ζ + 2πi` of the universal cover `exp : ℂ → ℂ \ {0}`. -/
theorem exp_add_two_pi_I' (ζ : ℂ) : Complex.exp (ζ + 2 * π * Complex.I) = Complex.exp ζ :=
  Complex.exp_periodic ζ

/-- **Holonomy.** Under the deck transformation the developing map is rotated by `e^{2πiβ}`. So the
transverse metric is the flat metric of the universal cover of `ℂ \ {0}` modulo the rotation by the
angle `2πβ`, i.e. the flat cone of angle `2πβ`. -/
theorem exp_mul_add_two_pi_I (β : ℝ) (ζ : ℂ) :
    Complex.exp (β * (ζ + 2 * π * Complex.I)) =
      Complex.exp ((2 * π * β : ℝ) * Complex.I) * Complex.exp (β * ζ) := by
  rw [← Complex.exp_add]
  congr 1
  push_cast
  ring

/-- The holonomy rotation is trivial exactly when `β` is an integer. So for `β ∉ ℤ` there is no
single-valued flat coordinate around the cone point. -/
theorem exp_two_pi_mul_I_eq_one_iff (β : ℝ) :
    Complex.exp ((2 * π * β : ℝ) * Complex.I) = 1 ↔ ∃ m : ℤ, β = m := by
  rw [Complex.exp_eq_one_iff]
  have hπ : (2 * π * Complex.I : ℂ) ≠ 0 := by simp [Real.pi_ne_zero]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨m, hm⟩
    refine ⟨m, ?_⟩
    have h : ((β : ℂ) - m) * (2 * π * Complex.I) = 0 := by
      rw [sub_mul, ← hm]
      push_cast
      ring
    have h' : (β : ℂ) = m := sub_eq_zero.mp ((mul_eq_zero.mp h).resolve_right hπ)
    exact_mod_cast h'
  · rintro ⟨m, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨m, by push_cast; ring⟩

/-! ### Metric invariants: the cone angle as circumference over radius -/

/-- The length, for the transverse cone metric, of the radial segment `t ↦ t e^{iθ}`,
`0 ≤ t ≤ r`, from the cone point to the circle `|z_0| = r`. The integrand is
`√(β² |z_0|^(2β-2) |γ'(t)|²)` with `γ'(t) = DΓ(t, θ)(1, 0)`. -/
noncomputable def coneRadialLength (β : ConeAngle) (θ r : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ∫ t in (0)..r, √(transverseConeMetric β (polarMap (t, θ)) (fderiv ℝ polarMap (t, θ) (1, 0)))

/-- The length, for the transverse cone metric, of the circle `θ ↦ r e^{iθ}`, `0 ≤ θ ≤ 2π`. -/
noncomputable def coneCircleLength (β : ConeAngle) (r : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ∫ θ in (0)..(2 * π),
    √(transverseConeMetric β (polarMap (r, θ)) (fderiv ℝ polarMap (r, θ) (0, 1)))

/-- **The circle `|z_0| = r` is at distance `ρ = r^β` from the cone point along rays.** -/
theorem coneRadialLength_eq (β : ConeAngle) (θ : ℝ) {r : ℝ} (hr : 0 ≤ r) :
    coneRadialLength β θ r = r ^ β.beta := by
  have hβ := β.pos
  have hcongr : EqOn
      (fun t : ℝ => √(transverseConeMetric β (polarMap (t, θ)) (fderiv ℝ polarMap (t, θ) (1, 0))))
      (fun t : ℝ => β.beta * t ^ (β.beta - 1)) (uIcc 0 r) := by
    intro t ht
    rw [uIcc_of_le hr] at ht
    have ht0 : 0 ≤ t := ht.1
    simp only
    rw [transverseConeMetric, norm_polarMap_of_nonneg (x := (t, θ)) ht0, normSq_fderiv_polarMap]
    simp only [one_pow, zero_pow two_ne_zero, mul_zero, add_zero, mul_one]
    have hsq : β.beta ^ 2 * t ^ (2 * β.beta - 2) = (β.beta * t ^ (β.beta - 1)) ^ 2 := by
      rw [mul_pow, ← Real.rpow_natCast (t ^ (β.beta - 1)), ← Real.rpow_mul ht0]
      norm_num
      ring_nf
      simp
    rw [hsq, Real.sqrt_sq (mul_nonneg hβ.le (Real.rpow_nonneg ht0 _))]
  rw [coneRadialLength, intervalIntegral.integral_congr hcongr, intervalIntegral.integral_const_mul,
    integral_rpow (Or.inl (by linarith))]
  rw [sub_add_cancel, Real.zero_rpow hβ.ne', sub_zero]
  field_simp

/-- **The circle `|z_0| = r` has length `2πβ r^β`.** -/
theorem coneCircleLength_eq (β : ConeAngle) {r : ℝ} (hr : 0 < r) :
    coneCircleLength β r = 2 * π * β.beta * r ^ β.beta := by
  have hβ := β.pos
  have hconst : ∀ θ : ℝ,
      √(transverseConeMetric β (polarMap (r, θ)) (fderiv ℝ polarMap (r, θ) (0, 1))) =
        β.beta * r ^ β.beta := by
    intro θ
    rw [transverseConeMetric, norm_polarMap_of_nonneg (x := (r, θ)) hr.le, normSq_fderiv_polarMap]
    simp only [one_pow, zero_pow two_ne_zero, mul_one, zero_add]
    have hsq : β.beta ^ 2 * r ^ (2 * β.beta - 2) * r ^ 2 = (β.beta * r ^ β.beta) ^ 2 := by
      rw [mul_pow, ← Real.rpow_natCast (r ^ β.beta), ← Real.rpow_mul hr.le,
        ← Real.rpow_natCast r 2, mul_assoc, ← Real.rpow_add hr]
      norm_num
      ring_nf
      simp
    rw [hsq, Real.sqrt_sq (mul_nonneg hβ.le (Real.rpow_nonneg hr.le _))]
  simp only [coneCircleLength, hconst, intervalIntegral.integral_const, sub_zero, smul_eq_mul]
  ring

/-- **The cone angle is `2πβ`:** circumference `= 2πβ ×` radius, for every circle around the
cone point. -/
theorem coneCircleLength_eq_two_pi_mul_radialLength (β : ConeAngle) (θ : ℝ) {r : ℝ}
    (hr : 0 < r) :
    coneCircleLength β r = 2 * π * β.beta * coneRadialLength β θ r := by
  rw [coneCircleLength_eq β hr, coneRadialLength_eq β θ hr.le]

end ConicalKahler
